---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';

// What the blog is, and who writes it.
//
// This route was the disclaimer until the header nav was cut back to Topics and
// About. The legal text moved to /disclaimer, which the footer links, and the
// route kept its path so nothing that pointed here 404s - it just arrives at an
// introduction now rather than at the small print, with a link on to it.
//
// Deliberately short. It is the one page on the site that is not an entry or a
// listing, and the writing is what the reader came for; a long biography here
// would be the only place on the blog talking about itself at length.
//
// Facts rather than positioning: the name, what gets written about, how it is
// filed, and where the terms are. Anything about an employer, a job title or a
// certification is left out on purpose - it dates, and none of it is what makes
// an entry here worth reading.
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About"
	description={`About ${SITE.name} and the Microsoft security engineering work published here.`}
	narrow
	crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About' }]}
>
	{
		/* Centred in the reading column, as the disclaimer and the entries are. `narrow`
	    on the layout is what lines the breadcrumb above it up with this copy rather
	    than with the far left of the 5xl main. */
	}
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
		{
			/* The heading is "About" and there is no eyebrow over it. It used to be the
			   other way round - an "About" eyebrow above the site's name as the h1 - which
			   put the name in the one slot on the page that should say what the page is.
			   Every other route here titles itself: Disclaimer, Projects, Solutions. The
			   name is in the masthead, the tab and the footer already.

			   No mt-1 on it either, because the margin existed to hold it off the eyebrow.
			   This is now the same two lines /disclaimer opens with. */
		}
		<h1 class="font-display text-text text-3xl font-bold">About</h1>

		<div class="prose-body mt-6">
			<p>
				This is a personal blog about Microsoft security engineering, with a particular focus on
				Microsoft XDR, identity and detection engineering.
			</p>

			<p>
				It documents practical work with Microsoft Defender XDR, Microsoft Sentinel, Microsoft Entra
				ID and related security technologies, including investigations, KQL queries, detections,
				security configurations, lab work and projects.
			</p>

			<p>
				The focus is on how these technologies are implemented and used in practice, rather than
				repeating product documentation. Articles document what I built or investigated, the
				approach I took, the reasoning behind technical decisions, and any limitations, trade-offs
				or unexpected behaviour encountered along the way.
			</p>

			<h2>Articles and projects</h2>

			<p>
				Articles cover individual technical subjects, investigations and implementations. They are
				organised primarily by <a href={withBase('/solutions')}>solution</a>, making it easy to find
				work involving a particular Microsoft security technology, with topics providing additional
				context such as Conditional Access, KQL, detection engineering and identity security.
			</p>

			<p>
				<a href={withBase('/projects')}>Projects</a> document more substantial pieces of practical work,
				bringing together the design, implementation and testing of a solution from the initial problem
				through to the finished result.
			</p>

			{
				/* {' '} and not a plain line break before the link. Astro drops the
				   whitespace between text and an element that starts a line, so "see the"
				   ran straight into "Disclaimer" with nothing between them. The other two
				   links in this page keep their space by sitting on the same line as the
				   word beside them, which works until Prettier reflows the paragraph -
				   this is the form that does not depend on where the line happens to break.
				   Same idiom as the empty-state copy in index.astro. */
			}
			<p>
				This is an independent personal blog documenting my own work and learning. For information
				about accuracy, liability, trademarks and use of the material, see the{' '}
				<a href={withBase('/disclaimer')}>Disclaimer</a>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
